          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Consider 4 points A, B, C, D in the plane with no three collinear. Answer the following questions. Some answers may require you to consider different cases, depending on how the points are positioned in the plane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.414,
            0.881,
            0.453
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) How many different quadrilaterals do they form if the quadrilateral is allowed to be self-intersecting or non-convex?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.453,
            0.881,
            0.494
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) How many of these quadrilaterals are self-intersecting? How many are convex?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.502,
            0.881,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. Suppose P is a point on side AB of ∆ABC and the line through P parallel to BC meets AC in point Q. For parts (i) to (iii), assume "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AP} = 1, \\mathrm{AQ} = \\sqrt{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and see Fig. 12.39."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.572,
            0.863,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.129,
                0.572,
                0.863,
                0.696
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_27_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.451,
                0.703,
                0.549,
                0.721
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 12.39"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.73,
            0.705,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) If PB = 2 find QC. ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " See the dotted line)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.755,
            0.713,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*(ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { I f }   \\mathrm { P } \\bar { \\mathrm { B } } = \\frac { 1 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " find QC. ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " See the dotted lines)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.785,
            0.424,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*(iii) If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P B } = { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " find QC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.812,
            0.659,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Divide both PB and AP suitably.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.837,
            0.88,
            0.918
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*(iv) Show that if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { A P } } { \\mathrm { P B } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a rational number, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AP}}{\\mathrm{PB}} = \\frac{\\mathrm{AQ}}{\\mathrm{QC}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . In Grade 10, you will prove this equality without assuming "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { A P } } { \\mathrm { P B } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is rational. That will require a new idea."
            }
          ]
        }
